###
# Tenant Guards Smoke Test
# Tests tenant authentication on protected endpoints
# Base URL: http://localhost:3000
#
# Prerequisites:
# - Server running: npm run dev
# - Replace <TENANT_ID> with a valid tenant ID from database
# - Replace <INTERNAL_TOKEN> with INTERNAL_API_TOKEN from .env (if set)
###

### 1. POST /api/simulate WITHOUT headers
# Expected: 400 (Missing x-tenant-id header)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/simulate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "destinationCep": "01001000",
  "quantity": 5
}

### 2. POST /api/simulate WITH tenant headers
# Expected: 200 (Success with freight calculation)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/simulate
Content-Type: application/json
x-tenant-id: <TENANT_ID>
x-internal-token: <INTERNAL_TOKEN>

{
  "destinationCep": "01001000",
  "quantity": 5
}

### 3. GET /api/history WITHOUT headers
# Expected: 400 (Missing x-tenant-id header)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/history

### 4. GET /api/history WITH tenant headers
# Expected: 200 (Success with simulation history)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/history
x-tenant-id: <TENANT_ID>
x-internal-token: <INTERNAL_TOKEN>

### 5. GET /api/metrics/overview WITHOUT headers
# Expected: 400 (Missing x-tenant-id header)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/metrics/overview

### 6. GET /api/metrics/overview WITH tenant headers
# Expected: 200 (Success with metrics data)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/metrics/overview
x-tenant-id: <TENANT_ID>
x-internal-token: <INTERNAL_TOKEN>

###
# Notes:
# - x-internal-token is optional (only if INTERNAL_API_TOKEN is set in .env)
# - All protected endpoints validate tenant context via getTenantContext()
# - Invalid tenant IDs will return 400 (Tenant not found)
# - Cache keys include tenant ID for proper isolation
###
